1. Backward Incompatible Changes
========================================

- Curl:
  . curl_multi_exec() now throws a TypeError when still_running is not an int.
  . Nested arrays in CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS now throw a TypeError, instead of being
    silently converted to the string "Array".

- PDO:
  . PDOStatement::bindColumn() now throws a ValueError when the column name is
    not present in the result set. It previously reported the condition
    through PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE and returned false.

- SOAP:
  . SoapClient no longer follows an HTTP redirect to a different origin
    (scheme, host, or port) and throws a SoapFault instead. Previously the
    request body and the configured credentials and headers were resent to
    the new origin. A redirect from http to https on the same host is still
    followed. Set the new follow_cross_origin_redirects option to true to
    restore the previous behavior.

- Session:
  . Setting session.cookie_path to a value containing one of ";\r\n", or
    session.cookie_domain to a value containing one of ",; \t\r\n\013\014",
    now emits a warning and leaves the setting unchanged. Previously such a
    value was appended to the Set-Cookie header verbatim, which let an
    application terminate one attribute and append further ones.

- Standard:
  . The number of filters that can be chained in a php://filter URL is limited
    to 16 by default. Set the stream context option max_filter_count to change
    this.

========================================
2. New Features
========================================

- Curl:
  . Multiple files can now be uploaded with the same field name by passing an
    array of CURLFile or CURLStringFile objects to CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS.

- Intl:
  . Locale::acceptFromHttp() and locale_accept_from_http() now accept an
    optional $availableLocales array argument. When given, the
    Accept-Language header is matched against these locales instead of all
    locales known to ICU, and the matching entry is returned as passed.
    A ValueError is thrown if the array is empty or contains an invalid
    locale, and a TypeError if it contains a non-string value.

- Streams:
  . The so_linger, so_rcvbuf and so_sndbuf stream socket context options are
    now also applied to unix and unix datagram sockets.

